1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,063
This tiny spoon could weigh a billion tons.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,476
No, seriously.

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:10,446
Somewhere in space, a star died.

4
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:14,125
Its core collapsed into something so dense...

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,706
That's a neutron star.

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,581
Imagine squeezing the mass of an entire mountain

7
00:00:18,581 --> 00:00:20,470
into something smaller than a city.

8
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:22,702
A teaspoon of its material would weigh

9
00:00:22,702 --> 00:00:24,535
around a billion tons on Earth.

10
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,604
That's not even the craziest part.

11
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:27,917
Some neutron stars spin

12
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:29,935
hundreds of times every second.

13
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,372
And some shoot beams of radiation through space

14
00:00:32,372 --> 00:00:33,863
like a cosmic lighthouse.

15
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,073
They're called pulsars.

16
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:36,596
So next time you think space is just

17
00:00:36,596 --> 00:00:38,226
a bunch of pretty stars,

18
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:38,928
remember.

19
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:41,420
Somewhere out there, there's a star so dense

20
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,957
that a teaspoon of it weighs more than a mountain.

21
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:51,858
Space is ridiculous.

